----------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Colours
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

The app's colours and the guide's charts use the colour-universal-design
palette of Masataka Okabe and Kei Ito (the Okabe-Ito palette), chosen because
people with common colour-vision differences can tell its colours apart.
Long-Horizon never uses colour as the only cue.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Fonts in the guide PDF
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

The repository ships no font files; the app uses the fonts of your system.
docs/Long-Horizon-Guide.pdf embeds subsets of Lora (Cyreal), Inter
(Rasmus Andersson) and, for code, Liberation Mono, all under the SIL Open Font License
1.1 (https://openfontlicense.org), when those fonts are installed on the
machine that builds it (tools/build-pdf.py lists the embedded fonts).

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Methods from published research
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Task procedures were re-implemented from the method descriptions of the
published papers, in our own words. No code, test items, figures or text were
copied from them. The main sources: Cao, Zhang, Zhang, Zhang & Zhang 2026
(executive n-back); Wang, Sun & Xiao 2025 (Equal Steps); Jaeggi, Buschkuehl,
Jonides & Perrig 2008 (dual n-back); Laine, Fellman, Waris & Nyman 2018
(n-back lures and the grouping strategy); Oberauer, Suess, Wilhelm & Wittmann
2008, Chuderski 2014, Bateman, Thompson & Birney 2019 and Li & Birney 2026
(relation monitoring); Unsworth, Heitz, Schrock & Engle 2005 (automated
operation span); Jastrzebski, Ociepka & Chuderski 2023 (Graph Mapping);
Matzen et al. 2010 (Sandia-type matrix rules); Jacobson & Truax 1991
(reliable change). Full references are in the guide, chapter 13.

Long-Horizon contains no code, configuration or statistics formats, help text,
sounds or images from Brain Workshop (GPL) or from tools under CC BY-NC or
AGPL licences, and no items from copyrighted tests such as Raven's matrices,
ICAR, WAIS or LSAC.

Dual n-back in Long-Horizon presents positions and sounds as two independent
streams. Long-Horizon never asks users to pick on-screen text that matches an
earlier spoken item (cf. US patent 8,408,915). This note is not legal advice.
